Since Friday Sep, 11 we started seeing session timeouts in Zookeeper and connection errors from the kafka brokers to Zookeeper. That required a few restarts of Kafka over the weekend before we could investigate the issue.

The relevant message from the Zookeeper logs seems to be:

{noformat}
[2020-09-12 16:34:20,032] INFO Creating new log file: log.7c00000001 (org.apache.zookeeper.server.persistence.FileTxnLog)
[2020-09-12 16:34:21,452] WARN fsync-ing the write ahead log in SyncThread:2 took 1415ms which will adversely effect operation latency. File size is 67108880 bytes. See the ZooKeeper troubleshooting guide (org.apache.zookeeper.server.persistence.FileTxnLog)
{noformat}

which is present even after a restart.

My interpretation is that this fsync operation might exceed the Zookeeper session timeout. The session timeout is controlled by

{noformat}
     ZOOKEEPER_TICK_TIME:                    2000
{noformat}

which is 2000ms by default and might be causing the timeouts and connection errors we were seeing. I've set this parameter to 8000ms

{noformat}
INFO Created server with tickTime 8000 minSessionTimeout 16000 maxSessionTimeout 160000 datadir /var/lib/zookeeper/log/version-2 snapdir /var/lib/zookeeper/data/version-2 (org.apache.zookeeper.server.ZooKeeperServer)
{noformat}

I'll keep monitoring the cluster, but the initial WARNING message is gone after we applied the new configuration.

