The current behavior of {{newinstall.sh}} is to preserve the value of a pre-existing {{EUPS_PKGROOT}} in the {{loadLSST*}} scripts.  This can result in the initial {{EUPS_PKGROOT}} becoming "stuck" when an end-user attempts to update their env unless they manually {{unset EUPS_PKGROOT}} or use a clean shell env.  Eg.

{code:java}
newinstall.sh -cbt
source ./loadLSST.sh # defines EUPS_PKGROOT

# rerunning newinstsall.sh to update env
newinstall.sh -cbt
source ./loadLSST.sh # original EUPS_PKGROOT value is preserved 
{code}

This should not be the default behavior but it may be useful in some cases, so it may be worth adding a cli switch to enable preserving {[EUPS_PKGROOT}}

