Qserv logger must be easilly configurable.
Next technique, base on log4cxx documentation allows to do it easily.

Example:

In QuerySession.cc, initialize a static logger:
{code:c++}
namespace lsst {
namespace qserv {
namespace qproc {

LOG_LOGGER QuerySession::_logger = LOG_GET("qserv.qproc.QuerySession");
{code}

then use it in Query session member functions:

{code:c++}
        if (LOG_CHECK_LVL(_logger, LOG_LVL_DEBUG)) {
            std::ostringstream stream;
            _showFinal(stream);
            LOGF(_logger, LOG_LVL_DEBUG, "Query Plugins applied:\n %1%" % stream.str());
        }
{code}

And log4cxx.property allow to easily configure logging for each Qserv module class:

{code}
# root logger level should be inherited by default
# this could be generalized to all Qserv modules:
log4j.logger.qproc=INFO
# can also be done at the class level for advanced debugging
#log4j.logger.qproc.QuerySession=DEBUG
{code}

